-- Quasi-coherence and section-localisation infrastructure, Serre Section 4.
-- QC models use actual canonical direct images and actual associated sheaves;
-- the existential atlas is truncated one universe above the section carriers.
-- Maps, finite sheaf diagrams, exactness descent, scalar restriction and the
-- concrete associated basic-member equivalence use their named interfaces.
-- Structural module/sheaf/scalar records and small type aliases remain open
-- to expose carriers; no quotient, ring-localisation, function-extensionality
-- or gluing proof construction is reopened by these client declarations.
-- The compact-open/global section-localisation theorem is not asserted here:
-- basic-member linearity, canonical-map identification and diagram squares
-- remain explicit continuation obligations.
